    "parent_status": "TO RESEARCH",
    "priority": 42,
    "scope": "Represented prime fields; canonical N-vector; dyadic N>=4 dividing p-1; exact supplied-root finite-boundary family recognition and all-output positive-sign q-Fourier evaluation; separate caller-authorized any-returned-root acquisition contract.",
    "deterministic_supplied_root_bound": "T_prime(p) + O(N*b^2 + b^3) in a bit-charged random-access model.",
    "reference_primality": "Actually executed deterministic trial division, charged T_prime(p)=O((1+sqrt(p))*b^2), which can dominate exponentially in b; no fast primality certificate is claimed.",
    "decline_scope": "Rank-four DECLINE concerns only the family for exact supplied/returned q, not membership in the union over primitive roots. No general fallback is implemented.",
    "any_root_acquisition": "Almost-sure zero-error acquisition of some primitive q under independent unbiased bits: expected O(b^3) arithmetic bit work and <=4b supplied bits, plus actual provider setup/work tariff; no finite uncapped deterministic worst-case bound.",
    "diagnostics": "Frozen API always counts; no disable switch exists. Add O((t*b+d)*log(t*b+d+2)) counter work and O(log(t*b+d+2)) counter storage to O(t*b^3+d*b) counter-free acquisition and provider costs. Expected bound survives geometric tails.",
    "caps": "T-candidate cap alone leaves raw draws unbounded and has failure 2^(-T). A D-raw-draw cap has failure (1-r)^D<=(3/4)^D, r=(p-1)/2^(b+1), at most D*b supplied bits, O(D*b^3) arithmetic plus O((D*b+D)*log(D*b+D+2)) conservative diagnostic work, provider and cap/input encoding costs. With both caps, 2^(-T)+(3/4)^D is an upper bound, not either separate exact equality. Zero caps return ROOT_LIMIT.",
    "root_limit": "Search budget exhausted only; neither root infeasibility nor family rejection.",
    "inversions_at_most": 6,
    "output_encoding": "For caller-known p,N and width ceil(b/8), ACCEPT is 1+(N+1)*ceil(b/8) bytes including q and all N residues; DECLINE is 1+ceil(b/8) bytes including q; ROOT_LIMIT is one byte. encode_result must be invoked; evaluate does not itself return the wire encoding.",
    "preserved_obligations": "Canonical input reading, supplied-root validation, failed family recognition, finite endpoint residual, singular source/target solves and anchor, provider work, diagnostics, cap encodings and complete output encoding remain paid.",
    "not_claimed": [
      "arbitrary-input FFT acceleration",
      "practical speed",
      "new algorithmic mechanism",
      "historical novelty",
      "unavailable prescribed-root acquisition",
      "all represented fields",
      "numerical stability",
      "whole-owner closure"
    ],
    "review_controls": "Stored independent controls only: 1825 vectors; 1545 accepts; 280 rank-four declines; 23264 checked coordinates; 988 singular recoveries; 1231 nonzero boundaries; at most six inversions. Finite controls corroborate, not replace, the proof.",
    "packaging_scientific_execution": false,
    "turnkey_scientific_replay_certified": false,
    "authority": "Read the included independent review and verdict with these mandatory clarifications; frozen candidate documents are historical originals, not authority for a diagnostic-disable switch or a complete bare O(D*b^3) arbitrary-cap diagnostic bound."
  },
